    </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <div class=\"q-card\">\n          <div class=\"q-header\" onclick=\"toggleQ(this)\">\n            <div class=\"q-num\">4</div>\n            <div class=\"q-title\">Construct an NFA over Σ = {0,1} accepting strings where the second-to-last symbol is '1'. Then give the equivalent DFA.</div>\n            <div class=\"q-meta\"><span class=\"marks-badge\">2 Marks</span><span class=\"co-badge\">CO2</span></div>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"q-body\" style=\"display:none\">\n            <p>RE: (0+1)*1(0+1)</p>\n            <button class=\"toggle-ans\" onclick=\"toggleAns(this)\">Show Answer</button>\n            <div class=\"q-ans\" style=\"display:none\">\n              <div class=\"q-ans-label\">Answer</div>\n              <strong>NFA (3 states):</strong>\n              <div class=\"tbl-wrap mt8\">\n                <table><thead><tr><th>State</th><th>0</th><th>1</th><th>Accept?</th></tr></thead>\n                <tbody>\n                  <tr><td><span class=\"td-start\">→ q₀</span></td><td>{q₀}</td><td>{q₀,q₁}</td><td></td></tr>\n                  <tr><td>q₁</td><td>{q₂}</td><td>{q₂}</td><td></td></tr>\n                  <tr><td>q₂</td><td>∅</td><td>∅</td><td class=\"td-acc\">✓</td></tr>\n                </tbody></table>\n              </div>\n              <strong>Equivalent DFA (subset construction):</strong> States {q₀}, {q₀,q₁}, {q₀,q₂}, {q₀,q₁,q₂} — start={q₀}, accept=any containing q₂.\n            </div>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <div class=\"q-card\">\n          <div class=\"q-header\" onclick=\"toggleQ(this)\">\n            <div class=\"q-num\">5</div>\n            <div class=\"q-title\">Convert the given ε-NFA to DFA: States {q₀,q₁,q₂}. q₀→ε→q₁, q₁→ε→q₂. q₀:0→q₀. q₁:1→q₁. q₂: 0,1→q₂ (accept). Σ={0,1}.</div>\n            <div class=\"q-meta\"><span class=\"marks-badge\">4 Marks</span><span class=\"co-badge\">CO2</span></div>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"q-body\" style=\"display:none\">\n            <button class=\"toggle-ans\" onclick=\"toggleAns(this)\">Show Answer</button>\n            <div class=\"q-ans\" style=\"display:none\">\n              <div class=\"q-ans-label\">Answer</div>\n              <strong>ε-closures:</strong> ε-cl(q₀)={q₀,q₁,q₂}, ε-cl(q₁)={q₁,q₂}, ε-cl(q₂)={q₂}<br>\n              <strong>DFA start state:</strong> A = ε-cl(q₀) = {q₀,q₁,q₂} (accepting, contains q₂)<br>\n              <div class=\"tbl-wrap mt8\">\n                <table><thead><tr><th>DFA</th><th>NFA States</th><th>0</th><th>1</th><th>Accept?</th></tr></thead>\n                <tbody>\n                  <tr><td><span class=\"td-start\">A</span></td><td>{q₀,q₁,q₂}</td><td>A</td><td>A</td><td class=\"td-acc\">✓</td></tr>\n                </tbody></table>\n              </div>\n              Since A transitions to itself on 0 and 1 and is accepting, this DFA has just 1 state: it accepts everything! Language = (0+1)* = all binary strings.\n            </div>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <div class=\"q-card\">\n          <div class=\"q-header\" onclick=\"toggleQ(this)\">\n            <div class=\"q-num\">6</div>\n            <div class=\"q-title\">Convert the given Moore Machine to Mealy Machine. Moore states: A/0, B/0, C/1, D/0. Start=A. Transitions: A:0→B, A:1→C | B:0→A, B:1→D | C:0→D, C:1→A | D:0→C, D:1→B.</div>\n            <div class=\"q-meta\"><span class=\"marks-badge\">4 Marks</span><span class=\"co-badge\">CO2</span></div>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"q-body\" style=\"display:none\">\n            <button class=\"toggle-ans\" onclick=\"toggleAns(this)\">Show Answer</button>\n            <div class=\"q-ans\" style=\"display:none\">\n              <div class=\"q-ans-label\">Answer — Moore → Mealy</div>\n              Rule: For each transition p →(a)→ q, Mealy output = Moore output of q = λ(q).<br>\n              <div class=\"tbl-wrap mt8\">\n                <table><thead><tr><th>State</th><th>Input</th><th>Mealy Output</th><th>Next State</th></tr></thead>\n                <tbody>\n                  <tr><td><span class=\"td-start\">→ A</span></td><td>0</td><td>λ(B)=0</td><td>B</td></tr>\n                  <tr><td>A</td><td>1</td><td>λ(C)=<span style=\"color:var(--amber)\">1</span></td><td>C</td></tr>\n                  <tr><td>B</td><td>0</td><td>λ(A)=0</td><td>A</td></tr>\n                  <tr><td>B</td><td>1</td><td>λ(D)=0</td><td>D</td></tr>\n                  <tr><td>C</td><td>0</td><td>λ(D)=0</td><td>D</td></tr>\n                  <tr><td>C</td><td>1</td><td>λ(A)=0</td><td>A</td></tr>\n                  <tr><td>D</td><td>0</td><td>λ(C)=<span style=\"color:var(--amber)\">1</span></td><td>C</td></tr>\n                  <tr><td>D</td><td>1</td><td>λ(B)=0</td><td>B</td></tr>\n                </tbody></table>\n              </div>\n            </div>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n\n      <!-- ═══ PAPER 3 ═══ -->\n      <div class=\"paper-content\" id=\"paper-2\">\n        <div class=\"alert info mb4\"><div class=\"alert-icon\">📋</div><div><strong>Paper 3 — Minimization & Regular Expressions Focus</strong> | Total: 14 Marks</div></div>\n\n        <div class=\"q-card\">\n          <div class=\"q-header\" onclick=\"toggleQ(this)\">\n            <div class=\"q-num\">1a</div>\n            <div class=\"q-title\">State the formal definition of a DFA. What does L(M) represent?</div>\n            <div class=\"q-meta\"><span class=\"marks-badge\">1 Mark</span><span class=\"co-badge\">CO1</span></div>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"q-body\" style=\"display:none\">\n            <button class=\"toggle-ans\" onclick=\"toggleAns(this)\">Show Answer</button>\n            <div class=\"q-ans\" style=\"display:none\">\n              <div class=\"q-ans-label\">Answer</div>\n              DFA M = (Q, Σ, δ, q₀, F) where Q=states, Σ=alphabet, δ:Q×Σ→Q (transition), q₀=start state, F⊆Q=accepting states.<br>\n              L(M) = {w ∈ Σ* | δ̂(q₀, w) ∈ F} — the set of all strings accepted by M; the language recognized by M.\n            </div>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <div class=\"q-card\">\n          <div class=\"q-header\" onclick=\"toggleQ(this)\">\n            <div class=\"q-num\">1b</div>\n            <div class=\"q-title\">If Σ = {a,b}, write 5 elements each of Σ² and Σ³. What is |Σ*|?</div>\n            <div class=\"q-meta\"><span class=\"marks-badge\">1 Mark</span><span class=\"co-badge\">CO1</span></div>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"q-body\" style=\"display:none\">\n            <button class=\"toggle-ans\" onclick=\"toggleAns(this)\">Show Answer</button>\n            <div class=\"q-ans\" style=\"display:none\">\n              <div class=\"q-ans-label\">Answer</div>\n              Σ² = {aa, ab, ba, bb} (all 4 — only 4 total)<br>\n              Σ³ = {aaa, aab, aba, abb, baa, bab, bba, bbb} (all 8)<br>\n              |Σ*| = ∞ (infinite — all strings of all lengths)\n            </div>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <div class=\"q-card\">\n          <div class=\"q-header\" onclick=\"toggleQ(this)\">\n            <div class=\"q-num\">2</div>\n            <div class=\"q-title\">Write Regular Expressions for: (a) Strings over {0,1} starting with 1 and ending with 0. (b) Strings over {a} with odd number of a's.</div>\n            <div class=\"q-meta\"><span class=\"marks-badge\">2 Marks</span><span class=\"co-badge\">CO1</span></div>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"q-body\" style=\"display:none\">\n            <button class=\"toggle-ans\" onclick=\"toggleAns(this)\">Show Answer</button>\n            <div class=\"q-ans\" style=\"display:none\">\n              <div class=\"q-ans-label\">Answer</div>\n              (a) Starts with 1, ends with 0: <code>1(0+1)*0</code><br>\n              Special case: \"10\" must also be included — covered since (0+1)* includes ε.<br>\n              (b) Odd number of a's: <code>a(aa)*</code><br>\n              (one a, then any number of pairs of a's)\n            </div>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <div class=\"q-card\">\n          <div class=\"q-header\" onclick=\"toggleQ(this)\">\n            <div class=\"q-num\">3</div>\n            <div class=\"q-title\">Construct a DFA over Σ = {a,b} that accepts all strings NOT containing \"aa\" as a substring.</div>\n            <div class=\"q-meta\"><span class=\"marks-badge\">2 Marks</span><span class=\"co-badge\">CO2</span></div>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"q-body\" style=\"display:none\">\n            <button class=\"toggle-ans\" onclick=\"toggleAns(this)\">Show Answer</button>\n            <div class=\"q-ans\" style=\"display:none\">\n              <div class=\"q-ans-label\">Answer — 3 States</div>\n              <div class=\"tbl-wrap\">\n                <table><thead><tr><th>State</th><th>Meaning</th><th>a</th><th>b</th><th>Accept?</th></tr></thead>\n                <tbody>\n                  <tr><td><span class=\"td-start\">→ q₀</span></td><td>Start / last was b</td><td>q₁</td><td>q₀</td><td class=\"td-acc\">✓</td></tr>\n                  <tr><td>q₁</td><td>Last was a</td><td>q₂</td><td>q₀</td><td class=\"td-acc\">✓</td></tr>\n                  <tr><td>q₂</td><td>Seen \"aa\" (dead)</td><td>q₂</td><td>q₂</td><td class=\"td-rej\">✗</td></tr>\n                </tbody></table>\n              </div>\n              Both q₀ and q₁ accept (we haven't seen \"aa\"). q₂ is dead (once \"aa\" seen, always reject).\n            </div>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <div class=\"q-card\">\n          <div class=\"q-header\" onclick=\"toggleQ(this)\">\n            <div class=\"q-num\">4</div>\n            <div class=\"q-title\">Construct an NFA over Σ = {0,1} accepting strings where the 3rd symbol from the right end is '1'. Give the equivalent regular expression.</div>\n            <div class=\"q-meta\"><span class=\"marks-badge\">2 Marks</span><span class=\"co-badge\">CO2</span></div>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"q-body\" style=\"display:none\">\n            <button class=\"toggle-ans\" onclick=\"toggleAns(this)\">Show Answer</button>\n            <div class=\"q-ans\" style=\"display:none\">\n              <div class=\"q-ans-label\">Answer</div>\n              RE: <code>(0+1)*1(0+1)(0+1)</code><br>\n              <strong>NFA (4 states):</strong>\n              <div class=\"tbl-wrap mt8\">\n                <table><thead><tr><th>State</th><th>0</th><th>1</th><th>Accept?</th></tr></thead>\n                <tbody>\n                  <tr><td><span class=\"td-start\">→ q₀</span></td><td>{q₀}</td><td>{q₀,q₁}</td><td></td></tr>\n                  <tr><td>q₁</td><td>{q₂}</td><td>{q₂}</td><td></td></tr>\n                  <tr><td>q₂</td><td>{q₃}</td><td>{q₃}</td><td></td></tr>\n                  <tr><td>q₃</td><td>∅</td><td>∅</td><td class=\"td-acc\">✓</td></tr>\n                </tbody></table>\n              </div>\n            </div>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <div class=\"q-card\">\n          <div class=\"q-header\" onclick=\"toggleQ(this)\">\n            <div class=\"q-num\">5</div>\n            <div class=\"q-title\">Minimize the DFA: States {A,B,C,D,E,F}. Start=A, Accept={C,F}. Σ={0,1}. A:0→B,1→D | B:0→C,1→E | C:0→C,1→C | D:0→E,1→B | E:0→F,1→A | F:0→F,1→F.</div>\n            <div class=\"q-meta\"><span class=\"marks-badge\">4 Marks</span><span class=\"co-badge\">CO2</span></div>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"q-body\" style=\"display:none\">\n            <button class=\"toggle-ans\" onclick=\"toggleAns(this)\">Show Answer</button>\n            <div class=\"q-ans\" style=\"display:none\">\n              <div class=\"q-ans-label\">Answer</div>\n              <strong>Step 1:</strong> Base marking — (accept vs non-accept) — mark pairs with one in {C,F} and one in {A,B,D,E}.<br>\n              <strong>Step 2:</strong> Check (C,F): C:0→C (accept), F:0→F (accept) — OK. C:1→C (accept), F:1→F (accept) — OK. → C ≡ F<br>\n              Check (A,D): A:0→B, D:0→E → need to check (B,E). B:0→C (accept), E:0→F (accept) — same class. B:1→E, D:1→B → (E,B)=(B,E) — also check. B:1→E (non-acc), E:1→A (non-acc) — same group. → B ≡ E and A ≡ D.<br>\n              <strong>Equivalence classes:</strong> {A,D}, {B,E}, {C,F}<br>\n              <strong>Minimized DFA (3 states):</strong>\n              <div class=\"tbl-wrap mt8\">\n                <table><thead><tr><th>State</th><th>0</th><th>1</th><th>Accept?</th></tr></thead>\n                <tbody>\n                  <tr><td><span class=\"td-start\">→ {A,D}</span></td><td>{B,E}</td><td>{B,E}</td><td></td></tr>\n                  <tr><td>{B,E}</td><td>{C,F}</td><td>{A,D}</td><td></td></tr>\n                  <tr><td>{C,F}</td><td>{C,F}</td><td>{C,F}</td><td class=\"td-acc\">✓</td></tr>\n                </tbody></table>\n              </div>\n            </div>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <div class=\"q-card\">\n          <div class=\"q-header\" onclick=\"toggleQ(this)\">\n            <div class=\"q-num\">6</div>\n            <div class=\"q-title\">Prove that regular languages are closed under: (a) Complement, and (b) Intersection. Illustrate with examples.</div>\n            <div class=\"q-meta\"><span class=\"marks-badge\">4 Marks</span><span class=\"co-badge\">CO2</span></div>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"q-body\" style=\"display:none\">\n            <button class=\"toggle-ans\" onclick=\"toggleAns(this)\">Show Answer</button>\n            <div class=\"q-ans\" style=\"display:none\">\n              <div class=\"q-ans-label\">Answer</div>\n              <strong>(a) Complement:</strong> If L is regular, ∃ DFA M=(Q,Σ,δ,q₀,F) with L=L(M). Construct M'=(Q,Σ,δ,q₀,Q−F) — same DFA with accepting and non-accepting states swapped. M' accepts exactly Σ*−L = L̄. Since M' is a valid DFA, L̄ is regular. ✓<br><br>\n              <em>Example:</em> L = {even-length strings}. L̄ = {odd-length strings}. Both regular.<br><br>\n              <strong>(b) Intersection:</strong> L₁∩L₂ = L̄₁ ∪ L̄₂ (by De Morgan's law). Since regular languages are closed under complement and union, they are also closed under intersection. ✓<br><br>\n              <em>Direct method (Cross-product construction):</em> Build DFA M=(Q₁×Q₂, Σ, δ, (q₁,q₂), F₁×F₂) where δ((p₁,p₂),a)=(δ₁(p₁,a),δ₂(p₂,a)). Accept only when both components are accepting.\n            </div>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n\n      <!-- ═══ PAPER 4 ═══ -->\n      <div class=\"paper-content\" id=\"paper-3\">\n        <div class=\"alert info mb4\"><div class=\"alert-icon\">📋</div><div><strong>Paper 4 — Comprehensive / Mixed</strong> | Total: 14 Marks | Hardest of the 4</div></div>\n\n        <div class=\"q-card\">\n          <div class=\"q-header\" onclick=\"toggleQ(this)\">\n            <div class=\"q-num\">1a</div>\n            <div class=\"q-title\">What is the Chomsky Hierarchy? Name the 4 grammar types and their corresponding automata.</div>\n            <div class=\"q-meta\"><span class=\"marks-badge\">1 Mark</span><span class=\"co-badge\">CO1</span></div>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"q-body\" style=\"display:none\">\n            <button class=\"toggle-ans\" onclick=\"toggleAns(this)\">Show Answer</button>\n            <div class=\"q-ans\" style=\"display:none\">\n              <div class=\"q-ans-label\">Answer</div>\n              <div class=\"tbl-wrap\">\n                <table><thead><tr><th>Type</th><th>Grammar</th><th>Language</th><th>Automaton</th></tr></thead>\n                <tbody>\n                  <tr><td>Type 0</td><td>Unrestricted</td><td>Recursively Enumerable</td><td>Turing Machine</td></tr>\n                  <tr><td>Type 1</td><td>Context-Sensitive</td><td>Context-Sensitive</td><td>Linear Bounded Automaton</td></tr>\n                  <tr><td>Type 2</td><td>Context-Free</td><td>Context-Free</td><td>Pushdown Automaton</td></tr>\n                  <tr><td>Type 3</td><td>Regular</td><td>Regular</td><td>Finite Automaton</td></tr>\n                </tbody></table>\n              </div>\n            </div>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <div class=\"q-card\">\n          <div class=\"q-header\" onclick=\"toggleQ(this)\">\n            <div class=\"q-num\">1b</div>\n            <div class=\"q-title\">For string w = \"baabb\", compute its reversal and list all substrings of length exactly 2.</div>\n            <div class=\"q-meta\"><span class=\"marks-badge\">1 Mark</span><span class=\"co-badge\">CO1</span></div>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"q-body\" style=\"display:none\">\n            <button class=\"toggle-ans\" onclick=\"toggleAns(this)\">Show Answer</button>\n            <div class=\"q-ans\" style=\"display:none\">\n              <div class=\"q-ans-label\">Answer</div>\n              w = b a a b b<br>\n              <strong>Reversal:</strong> wᴿ = b b a a b<br>\n              <strong>Substrings of length 2:</strong> ba, aa, ab, bb<br>\n              (consecutive pairs from w: b-a, a-a, a-b, b-b — 4 substrings, note \"ba\" appears once even though it could appear at positions 1 and would repeat if counting positions, but we list unique: {ba, aa, ab, bb})\n            </div>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <div class=\"q-card\">\n          <div class=\"q-header\" onclick=\"toggleQ(this)\">\n            <div class=\"q-num\">2</div>\n            <div class=\"q-title\">Let L = {aⁿbⁿ | n≥0} and R = a*b*. Is L regular? Is R regular? Compute L∩R and describe it.</div>\n            <div class=\"q-meta\"><span class=\"marks-badge\">2 Marks</span><span class=\"co-badge\">CO1</span></div>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"q-body\" style=\"display:none\">\n            <button class=\"toggle-ans\" onclick=\"toggleAns(this)\">Show Answer</button>\n            <div class=\"q-ans\" style=\"display:none\">\n              <div class=\"q-ans-label\">Answer</div>\n              <strong>L = {aⁿbⁿ | n≥0}:</strong> NOT regular — requires counting (pumping lemma proof would show this).<br>\n              <strong>R = a*b*:</strong> REGULAR — described by RE a*b*; DFA has 3 states (in-a's, in-b's, dead after b then a).<br>\n              <strong>L∩R:</strong> L⊆R already (every aⁿbⁿ is in a*b*), so L∩R = L = {aⁿbⁿ | n≥0}.<br>\n              This result is <strong>NOT regular</strong> — intersection of a non-regular and regular is not necessarily regular.\n            </div>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <div class=\"q-card\">\n          <div class=\"q-header\" onclick=\"toggleQ(this)\">\n            <div class=\"q-num\">3</div>\n            <div class=\"q-title\">Construct a DFA over Σ = {0,1} accepting strings that contain \"010\" as a substring.</div>\n            <div class=\"q-meta\"><span class=\"marks-badge\">2 Marks</span><span class=\"co-badge\">CO2</span></div>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"q-body\" style=\"display:none\">\n            <p>RE: (0+1)*010(0+1)*</p>\n            <button class=\"toggle-ans\" onclick=\"toggleAns(this)\">Show Answer</button>\n            <div class=\"q-ans\" style=\"display:none\">\n              <div class=\"q-ans-label\">Answer — 4 States</div>\n              <div class=\"tbl-wrap\">\n                <table><thead><tr><th>State</th><th>Meaning</th><th>0</th><th>1</th><th>Accept?</th></tr></thead>\n                <tbody>\n                  <tr><td><span class=\"td-start\">→ q₀</span></td><td>Start</td><td>q₁</td><td>q₀</td><td></td></tr>\n                  <tr><td>q₁</td><td>Saw \"0\"</td><td>q₁</td><td>q₂</td><td></td></tr>\n                  <tr><td>q₂</td><td>Saw \"01\"</td><td>q₃</td><td>q₀</td><td></td></tr>\n                  <tr><td>q₃</td><td>Saw \"010\"</td><td>q₃</td><td>q₃</td><td class=\"td-acc\">✓</td></tr>\n                </tbody></table>\n              </div>\n              q₃ is an absorbing accept state — once \"010\" is found, always accept.\n            </div>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <div class=\"q-card\">\n          <div class=\"q-header\" onclick=\"toggleQ(this)\">\n            <div class=\"q-num\">4</div>\n            <div class=\"q-title\">Write Regular Expressions for: (a) All strings over {a,b} that do NOT contain \"bb\" as substring. (b) Strings over {0,1} that represent even binary numbers (end in 0).</div>\n            <div class=\"q-meta\"><span class=\"marks-badge\">2 Marks</span><span class=\"co-badge\">CO1</span></div>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"q-body\" style=\"display:none\">\n            <button class=\"toggle-ans\" onclick=\"toggleAns(this)\">Show Answer</button>\n            <div class=\"q-ans\" style=\"display:none\">\n              <div class=\"q-ans-label\">Answer</div>\n              (a) No \"bb\": After every 'b' must come an 'a' (or end of string).<br>\n              RE: <code>(a + ba)*(b + ε)</code> or equivalently <code>(a+ba)*b?</code><br>\n              Explanation: (a+ba)* handles sequences where b is always followed by a; optional trailing b.<br><br>\n              (b) Even binary (ends in 0):<br>\n              RE: <code>(0+1)*0</code> — any string ending in 0 (includes \"0\" itself).<br>\n              Note: ε would represent 0 in value but the empty string doesn't end in 0.\n            </div>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <div class=\"q-card\">\n          <div class=\"q-header\" onclick=\"toggleQ(this)\">\n            <div class=\"q-num\">5</div>\n            <div class=\"q-title\">Convert the following ε-NFA to DFA using subset construction: States {q₀,q₁,q₂,q₃}. Start=q₀, Accept={q₃}. q₀:0→q₁,ε→q₂ | q₁:1→q₀,ε→q₃ | q₂:0→q₃ | q₃:1→q₂. Σ={0,1}.</div>\n            <div class=\"q-meta\"><span class=\"marks-badge\">4 Marks</span><span class=\"co-badge\">CO2</span></div>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"q-body\" style=\"display:none\">\n            <button class=\"toggle-ans\" onclick=\"toggleAns(this)\">Show Answer</button>\n            <div class=\"q-ans\" style=\"display:none\">\n              <div class=\"q-ans-label\">Answer</div>\n              <strong>ε-closures:</strong><br>\n              ε-cl(q₀) = {q₀, q₂} (q₀ →ε→ q₂)<br>\n              ε-cl(q₁) = {q₁, q₃} (q₁ →ε→ q₃)<br>\n              ε-cl(q₂) = {q₂}<br>\n              ε-cl(q₃) = {q₃}<br><br>\n              <strong>DFA Start:</strong> A = ε-cl(q₀) = {q₀,q₂} (contains q₀ and q₂ but not q₃, so NOT accepting)<br>\n              <div class=\"tbl-wrap mt8\">\n                <table><thead><tr><th>DFA</th><th>NFA States</th><th>0</th><th>1</th><th>Accept?</th></tr></thead>\n                <tbody>\n                  <tr><td><span class=\"td-start\">A</span></td><td>{q₀,q₂}</td><td>B</td><td>∅</td><td></td></tr>\n                  <tr><td>B</td><td>{q₁,q₃}</td><td>∅</td><td>C</td><td class=\"td-acc\">✓</td></tr>\n                  <tr><td>C</td><td>{q₀,q₂}</td><td>B</td><td>∅</td><td></td></tr>\n                  <tr><td>∅</td><td>{}</td><td>∅</td><td>∅</td><td></td></tr>\n                </tbody></table>\n              </div>\n              Note: A and C have the same NFA states → A ≡ C. Minimized: A→0→B→1→A (cycle), B accepts. Language: (0·1)* · 0 concatenated sequences.\n            </div>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <div class=\"q-card\">\n          <div class=\"q-header\" onclick=\"toggleQ(this)\">\n            <div class=\"q-num\">6</div>\n            <div class=\"q-title\">Design a Moore Machine over Σ={0,1} whose output at each state represents the remainder when the binary string read so far is divided by 3 (0, 1, or 2). Start from state representing remainder 0. Show transitions.</div>\n            <div class=\"q-meta\"><span class=\"marks-badge\">4 Marks</span><span class=\"co-badge\">CO2</span></div>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"q-body\" style=\"display:none\">\n            <button class=\"toggle-ans\" onclick=\"toggleAns(this)\">Show Answer</button>\n            <div class=\"q-ans\" style=\"display:none\">\n              <div class=\"q-ans-label\">Answer</div>\n              3 states: q₀(output:0), q₁(output:1), q₂(output:2) representing current value mod 3.<br>\n              When reading bit b, new value = (2 × current_value + b) mod 3.<br>\n              <div class=\"tbl-wrap mt8\">\n                <table><thead><tr><th>State (rem)</th><th>Output</th><th>On 0: (2×rem+0) mod 3</th><th>On 1: (2×rem+1) mod 3</th></tr></thead>\n                <tbody>\n                  <tr><td><span class=\"td-start\">→ q₀ (0)</span></td><td style=\"color:var(--green)\">0</td><td>q₀</td><td>q₁</td></tr>\n                  <tr><td>q₁ (1)</td><td>1</td><td>q₂</td><td>q₀</td></tr>\n                  <tr><td>q₂ (2)</td><td style=\"color:var(--amber)\">2</td><td>q₁</td><td>q₂</td></tr>\n                </tbody></table>\n              </div>\n              <em>Verify: 6 (binary 110): q₀→1→q₁→1→q₀→0→q₀, output at q₀ = 0. 6 mod 3 = 0 ✓</em>\n            </div>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div><!-- end papers section -->\n\n  </div><!-- end content -->\n</div><!-- end main -->\n\n<script>\n// ── Navigation Active State\nfunction setActive(el) {\n  document.querySelectorAll('.nav-item').forEach(i => i.classList.remove('active'));\n  el.classList.add('active');\n}\n\n// ── Paper Tabs\nfunction showPaper(idx) {\n  document.querySelectorAll('.paper-content').forEach((p,i) => {\n    p.classList.toggle('show', i === idx);\n  });\n  document.querySelectorAll('.paper-tab').forEach((t,i) => {\n    t.classList.toggle('active-tab', i === idx);\n  });\n}\n\n// ── Toggle Q body\nfunction toggleQ(header) {\n  const body = header.nextElementSibling;\n  if (!body) return;\n  body.style.display = body.style.display === 'none' ? 'block' : 'none';\n}\n\n// ── Toggle Answer\nfunction toggleAns(btn) {\n  const ans = btn.nextElementSibling;\n  if (!ans) return;\n  const showing = ans.style.display !== 'none';\n  ans.style.display = showing ? 'none' : 'block';\n  btn.textContent = showing ? 'Show Answer' : 'Hide Answer';\n}\n\n// ── Active nav on scroll\nconst sections = document.querySelectorAll('.section[id]');\nconst navItems = document.querySelectorAll('.nav-item[href]');\n\nconst observer = new IntersectionObserver((entries) => {\n  entries.forEach(entry => {\n    if (entry.isIntersecting) {\n      const id = '#' + entry.target.id;\n      navItems.forEach(item => {\n        item.classList.toggle('active', item.getAttribute('href') === id);\n      });\n    }\n  });\n}, { threshold: 0.2, rootMargin: '-80px 0px -60% 0px' });\n\nsections.forEach(s => observer.observe(s));\n</script>\n</body>\n</html>\n","Description":"Complete dark-themed TOC study website with notes, PYP solutions, and 4 sample papers.","Overwrite":false,"TargetFile":"C:\\Users\\tanus\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\TOC-Study-Hub\\index.html"}}]}
