{"step_index":61,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-05T16:43:57Z","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"ArtifactMetadata":{"RequestFeedback":false,"Summary":"Complete dark-themed TOC study website. Single HTML file with sidebar navigation, all Unit 1-3 notes, full PYP T1 solutions, and 4 sample question papers (6 questions each, show/hide answers). Dark color scheme with indigo/cyan accents.","UserFacing":false},"CodeContent":"<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n<meta charset=\"UTF-8\">\n<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\">\n<title>TOC Study Hub — Theory of Computation</title>\n<style>\n:root{\n  --bg:#07090f;--bg2:#0d1117;--bg3:#161b22;--bg4:#1c2128;--bg5:#21262d;\n  --sidebar:#080c14;--border:#21262d;--border2:#30363d;\n  --accent:#818cf8;--accent2:#6366f1;--cyan:#22d3ee;--amber:#fbbf24;\n  --green:#4ade80;--red:#f87171;--purple:#c084fc;\n  --text:#e6edf3;--text2:#b1bac4;--text3:#7d8590;\n  --active-bg:rgba(99,102,241,0.12);\n}\n*{margin:0;padding:0;box-sizing:border-box;}\nhtml{scroll-behavior:smooth;}\nbody{font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',system-ui,sans-serif;background:var(--bg);color:var(--text);display:flex;min-height:100vh;font-size:15px;line-height:1.7;}\n\n/* SIDEBAR */\n.sidebar{width:260px;min-width:260px;background:var(--sidebar);border-right:1px solid var(--border);position:sticky;top:0;height:100vh;overflow-y:auto;display:flex;flex-direction:column;z-index:100;scrollbar-width:thin;scrollbar-color:var(--bg5) transparent;}\n.sidebar::-webkit-scrollbar{width:4px;}.sidebar::-webkit-scrollbar-thumb{background:var(--bg5);border-radius:2px;}\n.logo{padding:20px 18px 14px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);display:flex;align-items:center;gap:10px;}\n.logo-icon{font-size:22px;}\n.logo-text{font-size:16px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:-.3px;}\n.logo-sub{font-size:11px;color:var(--text3);margin-top:1px;}\n.nav{padding:8px 0 20px;}\n.nav-group-title{padding:10px 18px 3px;font-size:10px;font-weight:700;color:var(--text3);text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.09em;}\n.nav-item{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:8px;padding:7px 18px;cursor:pointer;transition:.12s;font-size:13px;color:var(--text2);text-decoration:none;border-left:2px solid transparent;}\n.nav-item:hover{color:var(--text);background:rgba(255,255,255,.04);}\n.nav-item.active{color:var(--accent);background:var(--active-bg);border-left-color:var(--accent2);}\n.nav-item .ico{font-size:13px;min-width:15px;text-align:center;}\n.nav-sub .nav-item{padding-left:36px;font-size:12.5px;}\n\n/* MAIN */\n.main{flex:1;min-width:0;overflow-x:hidden;}\n.topbar{position:sticky;top:0;z-index:50;background:rgba(7,9,15,.88);backdrop-filter:blur(12px);border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);padding:11px 36px;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;}\n.topbar-title{font-size:13px;color:var(--text3);}\n.topbar-badge{font-size:11px;padding:3px 10px;border-radius:20px;background:rgba(99,102,241,.18);color:var(--accent);border:1px solid rgba(99,102,241,.3);font-weight:600;}\n.content{padding:40px 44px 80px;max-width:980px;}\n\n/* HERO */\n.hero{background:linear-gradient(135deg,#0d1117 0%,#121b30 60%,#0a1020 100%);border:1px solid var(--border2);border-radius:14px;padding:44px;margin-bottom:44px;position:relative;overflow:hidden;}\n.hero::before{content:'';position:absolute;top:-80px;right:-60px;width:280px;height:280px;background:radial-gradient(circle,rgba(99,102,241,.14) 0%,transparent 70%);}\n.hero-tag{display:inline-block;font-size:11px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--cyan);margin-bottom:10px;}\n.hero h1{font-size:34px;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:-.5px;margin-bottom:10px;background:linear-gradient(135deg,#e6edf3 30%,#818cf8 100%);-webkit-background-clip:text;-webkit-text-fill-color:transparent;background-clip:text;}\n.hero p{color:var(--text2);font-size:15px;max-width:540px;margin-bottom:24px;}\n.chips{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:8px;}\n.chip{padding:5px 14px;border-radius:20px;font-size:12px;font-weight:500;border:1px solid var(--border2);color:var(--text2);background:var(--bg3);}\n.chip.c1{border-color:rgba(34,211,238,.35);color:var(--cyan);}\n.chip.c2{border-color:rgba(129,140,248,.35);color:var(--accent);}\n.chip.c3{border-color:rgba(196,132,252,.35);color:var(--purple);}\n\n/* SECTIONS */\n.section{margin-bottom:60px;}\n.sec-head{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:10px;margin-bottom:24px;padding-bottom:14px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);}\n.sec-icon{font-size:20px;}\n.sec-title{font-size:21px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:-.3px;}\n.badge{font-size:11px;padding:2px 10px;border-radius:20px;font-weight:600;}\n.b-cyan{background:rgba(34,211,238,.1);color:var(--cyan);border:1px solid rgba(34,211,238,.22);}\n.b-ind{background:rgba(99,102,241,.1);color:var(--accent);border:1px solid rgba(99,102,241,.22);}\n.b-pur{background:rgba(196,132,252,.1);color:var(--purple);border:1px solid rgba(196,132,252,.22);}\n.b-amb{background:rgba(251,191,36,.1);color:var(--amber);border:1px solid rgba(251,191,36,.22);}\n.b-grn{background:rgba(74,222,128,.1);color:var(--green);border:1px solid rgba(74,222,128,.22);}\n\n/* CARDS */\n.card{background:var(--bg3);border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:10px;padding:20px 22px;margin-bottom:14px;}\n.ctitle{font-size:13.5px;font-weight:600;color:var(--accent);margin-bottom:10px;display:flex;align-items:center;gap:7px;}\n\n/* DEFINITION BOXES */\n.def{border-left:3px solid var(--accent2);background:rgba(99,102,241,.07);border-radius:0 8px 8px 0;padding:12px 16px;margin:10px 0;}\n.def.cy{border-left-color:var(--cyan);background:rgba(34,211,238,.06);}\n.def.am{border-left-color:var(--amber);background:rgba(251,191,36,.06);}\n.def.gr{border-left-color:var(--green);background:rgba(74,222,128,.06);}\n.def.rd{border-left-color:var(--red);background:rgba(248,113,113,.06);}\n.def-lbl{font-size:10.5px;font-weight:700;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.06em;color:var(--accent);margin-bottom:4px;}\n.def.cy .def-lbl{color:var(--cyan);}.def.am .def-lbl{color:var(--amber);}.def.gr .def-lbl{color:var(--green);}.def.rd .def-lbl{color:var(--red);}\n\n/* TABLES */\n.tw{overflow-x:auto;margin:10px 0;border-radius:8px;border:1px solid var(--border);}\ntable{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:13.5px;}\nthead tr{background:var(--bg4);}\nth{padding:9px 14px;text-align:left;font-weight:600;color:var(--text2);font-size:11.5px;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase;border-bottom:1px solid var(--border2);}\ntd{padding:8px 14px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);color:var(--text);}\ntr:last-child td{border-bottom:none;}\ntr:nth-child(even) td{background:rgba(255,255,255,.014);}\n.acc{color:var(--green);font-weight:600;}.rej{color:var(--red);}.strt{color:var(--amber);font-weight:600;}\n\n/* CODE */\npre,code{font-family:'JetBrains Mono','Fira Code',Consolas,monospace;}\n.cb{background:#040710;border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:8px;padding:14px 18px;margin:10px 0;overflow-x:auto;font-size:13px;line-height:1.8;color:#c9d1d9;}\ncode{background:rgba(255,255,255,.09);padding:2px 6px;border-radius:4px;font-size:13px;color:var(--cyan);}\n\n/* ALERTS */\n.alert{display:flex;gap:10px;padding:12px 14px;border-radius:8px;margin:12px 0;border:1px solid;font-size:13.5px;}\n.alert.tip{background:rgba(74,222,128,.05);border-color:rgba(74,222,128,.18);color:#c9f0d5;}\n.alert.warn{background:rgba(251,191,36,.05);border-color:rgba(251,191,36,.18);color:#fde8a0;}\n.alert.info{background:rgba(34,211,238,.05);border-color:rgba(34,211,238,.18);color:#a5f3fc;}\n.ai{font-size:15px;flex-shrink:0;margin-top:1px;}\n\n/* GRID */\n.g2{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:14px;margin:10px 0;}\n.g3{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr 1fr;gap:12px;margin:10px 0;}\n\n/* STAT */\n.sc{background:var(--bg3);border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:10px;padding:16px;text-align:center;}\n.sn{font-size:28px;font-weight:800;color:var(--accent);}\n.sl{font-size:12px;color:var(--text3);margin-top:3px;}\n\n/* FORMULA */\n.fm{font-family:monospace;background:var(--bg4);border:1px solid var(--border2);border-radius:6px;padding:9px 14px;margin:7px 0;font-size:14px;color:var(--amber);text-align:center;}\n\n/* SEP */\n.sep{border:none;border-top:1px solid var(--border);margin:28px 0;}\n\n/* SAMPLE PAPERS */\n.ptabs{display:flex;gap:8px;margin-bottom:20px;flex-wrap:wrap;}\n.ptab{padding:7px 18px;border-radius:8px;cursor:pointer;font-size:13px;font-weight:500;border:1px solid var(--border2);color:var(--text2);background:var(--bg3);transition:.13s;}\n.ptab:hover{border-color:var(--accent);color:var(--accent);}\n.ptab.at{background:var(--active-bg);border-color:var(--accent2);color:var(--accent);}\n.pc{display:none;}.pc.show{display:block;}\n\n/* Q CARDS */\n.qcard{background:var(--bg3);border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:10px;margin-bottom:12px;overflow:hidden;}\n.qhdr{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:10px;padding:13px 18px;background:var(--bg4);border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);cursor:pointer;user-select:none;}\n.qhdr:hover{background:var(--bg5);}\n.qnum{width:28px;height:28px;border-radius:50%;background:var(--bg5);display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-size:12px;font-weight:700;color:var(--accent);flex-shrink:0;}\n.qtxt{flex:1;font-size:13.5px;font-weight:500;color:var(--text);}\n.qmeta{display:flex;gap:7px;align-items:center;flex-shrink:0;}\n.mb2{font-size:11px;padding:2px 7px;border-radius:20px;font-weight:600;background:rgba(251,191,36,.1);color:var(--amber);border:1px solid rgba(251,191,36,.22);}\n.cb2{font-size:11px;padding:2px 7px;border-radius:20px;font-weight:600;background:rgba(34,211,238,.07);color:var(--cyan);border:1px solid rgba(34,211,238,.18);}\n.qbody{padding:18px;border-top:1px solid var(--border);}\n.qans{margin-top:10px;padding:13px;background:rgba(74,222,128,.04);border:1px solid rgba(74,222,128,.13);border-radius:8px;}\n.qans-lbl{font-size:10.5px;font-weight:700;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--green);margin-bottom:7px;letter-spacing:.06em;}\n.tbtn{margin-top:9px;padding:5px 14px;font-size:12px;cursor:pointer;background:transparent;border:1px solid var(--border2);border-radius:6px;color:var(--text3);font-family:inherit;transition:.13s;}\n.tbtn:hover{border-color:var(--green);color:var(--green);}\n\n/* PYP */\n.pyq{margin-bottom:18px;padding:18px 20px;background:var(--bg3);border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:10px;}\n.pyqh{display:flex;align-items:flex-start;gap:10px;margin-bottom:10px;}\n.pyqn{background:var(--accent2);color:white;padding:3px 9px;border-radius:20px;font-size:11.5px;font-weight:700;flex-shrink:0;margin-top:2px;}\n.pyqt{font-size:14px;font-weight:500;}\n.pya{margin-top:10px;padding:14px 16px;background:var(--bg4);border-radius:8px;border-left:3px solid var(--green);}\n.pyal{font-size:10.5px;font-weight:700;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--green);margin-bottom:8px;letter-spacing:.06em;}\n\nh2{font-size:17px;font-weight:700;margin:18px 0 9px;color:var(--text);}\nh3{font-size:14.5px;font-weight:600;margin:14px 0 7px;color:var(--text2);}\np{margin:7px 0;color:var(--text2);}\nul,ol{padding-left:19px;margin:7px 0;}\nli{margin:3px 0;color:var(--text2);}\nstrong{color:var(--text);font-weight:600;}\nem{color:var(--amber);font-style:normal;}\n.mt8{margin-top:8px;}.mt12{margin-top:12px;}.mt16{margin-top:16px;}\n.tc{color:var(--cyan);}.ta{color:var(--amber);}.tg{color:var(--green);}.tp{color:var(--purple);}\n\n.main::-webkit-scrollbar{width:5px;}.main::-webkit-scrollbar-thumb{background:var(--bg5);border-radius:3px;}\n\n@media(max-width:860px){.sidebar{width:220px;min-width:220px;}.content{padding:28px 20px 60px;}.g2{grid-template-columns:1fr;}.hero{padding:28px;}}\n@media(max-width:620px){body{flex-direction:column;}.sidebar{width:100%;height:auto;position:static;border-right:none;border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);}.nav{display:none;}.content{padding:20px 14px 60px;}.hero h1{font-size:26px;}}\n</style>\n</head>\n<body>\n\n<!-- SIDEBAR -->\n<nav class=\"sidebar\">\n  <div class=\"logo\">\n    <div class=\"logo-icon\">⚛</div>\n    <div>\n      <div class=\"logo-text\">TOC Study Hub</div>\n      <div class=\"logo-sub\">Theory of Computation · Sem 3</div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"nav\">\n    <div class=\"nav-group-title\">Overview</div>\n    <a href=\"#home\" class=\"nav-item active\" onclick=\"setActive(this)\"><span class=\"ico\">🏠</span>Home</a>\n\n    <div class=\"nav-group-title\" style=\"margin-top:6px\">Unit 1 — Introduction</div>\n    <a href=\"#u1-toc\" class=\"nav-item\" onclick=\"setActive(this)\"><span class=\"ico\">📐</span>Branches of ToC</a>\n    <a href=\"#u1-strings\" class=\"nav-item\" onclick=\"setActive(this)\"><span class=\"ico\">🔤</span>Alphabets &amp; Strings</a>\n    <a href=\"#u1-langs\" class=\"nav-item\" onclick=\"setActive(this)\"><span class=\"ico\">🌐</span>Language Operations</a>\n    <a href=\"#u1-math\" class=\"nav-item\" onclick=\"setActive(this)\"><span class=\"ico\">📏</span>Math Prerequisites</a>\n\n    <div class=\"nav-group-title\" style=\"margin-top:6px\">Unit 2 — Finite Automata</div>\n    <a href=\"#u2-dfa\" class=\"nav-item\" onclick=\"setActive(this)\"><span class=\"ico\">🤖</span>DFA</a>\n    <a href=\"#u2-nfa\" class=\"nav-item\" onclick=\"setActive(this)\"><span class=\"ico\">🔀</span>NFA &amp; ε-NFA</a>\n    <a href=\"#u2-convert\" class=\"nav-item\" onclick=\"setActive(this)\"><span class=\"ico\">🔄</span>NFA → DFA</a>\n    <a href=\"#u2-min\" class=\"nav-item\" onclick=\"setActive(this)\"><span class=\"ico\">📦</span>DFA Minimization</a>\n    <a href=\"#u2-mealy\" class=\"nav-item\" onclick=\"setActive(this)\"><span class=\"ico\">⚙️</span>Moore &amp; Mealy</a>\n    <a href=\"#u2-closure\" class=\"nav-item\" onclick=\"setActive(this)\"><span class=\"ico\">🔒</span>Closure Properties</a>\n\n    <div class=\"nav-group-title\" style=\"margin-top:6px\">Unit 3 — Regular Expr.</div>\n    <a href=\"#u3-def\" class=\"nav-item\" onclick=\"setActive(this)\"><span class=\"ico\">✨</span>RE Definition</a>\n    <a href=\"#u3-examples\" class=\"nav-item\" onclick=\"setActive(this)\"><span class=\"ico\">📋</span>RE Examples</a>\n    <a href=\"#u3-equiv\" class=\"nav-item\" onclick=\"setActive(this)\"><span class=\"ico\">⚖️</span>RE Equivalence</a>\n    <a href=\"#u3-fa\" class=\"nav-item\" onclick=\"setActive(this)\"><span class=\"ico\">↔️</span>RE ↔ Automata</a>\n\n    <div class=\"nav-group-title\" style=\"margin-top:6px\">Previous Year Paper</div>\n    <a href=\"#pyp\" class=\"nav-item\" onclick=\"setActive(this)\"><span class=\"ico\">📄</span>T1 — All Solutions</a>\n\n    <div class=\"nav-group-title\" style=\"margin-top:6px\">Sample Papers</div>\n    <a href=\"#papers\" class=\"nav-item\" onclick=\"setActive(this)\"><span class=\"ico\">📝</span>4 × 6 Question Papers</a>\n  </div>\n</nav>\n\n<!-- MAIN -->\n<div class=\"main\">\n  <div class=\"topbar\">\n    <div class=\"topbar-title\">TOC · Test 1 Prep · Units 1, 2, 3</div>\n    <div class=\"topbar-badge\">14 Marks Per Paper</div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"content\">\n\n    <!-- HOME -->\n    <div id=\"home\" class=\"section\">\n      <div class=\"hero\">\n        <div class=\"hero-tag\">📚 Exam Ready</div>\n        <h1>Theory of Computation</h1>\n        <p>Complete notes, previous year solutions, and 4 practice papers for Test 1. Covers Units 1–3 from your class lecture slides.</p>\n        <div class=\"chips\">\n          <span class=\"chip c1\">Unit 1 · Introduction</span>\n          <span class=\"chip c2\">Unit 2 · Finite Automata</span>\n          <span class=\"chip c3\">Unit 3 · Regular Expr.</span>\n          <span class=\"chip\">PYP T1 Full Solutions</span>\n          <span class=\"chip\">4 Sample Papers</span>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"g3\">\n        <div class=\"sc\"><div class=\"sn\" style=\"color:var(--cyan)\">3</div><div class=\"sl\">Units Covered</div></div>\n        <div class=\"sc\"><div class=\"sn\">6</div><div class=\"sl\">PYP Questions Solved</div></div>\n        <div class=\"sc\"><div class=\"sn\" style=\"color:var(--amber)\">24</div><div class=\"sl\">Sample Questions</div></div>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"alert tip mt16\"><div class=\"ai\">💡</div><div>Typical paper pattern: Q1a(1M) + Q1b(1M) + Q2(2M) + Q3(2M) + Q4(2M) + Q5(4M) + Q6(4M) = <strong>16 marks</strong>. Heavy focus on DFA construction, NFA→DFA, and minimization.</div></div>\n    </div>\n\n    <!-- U1 TOC -->\n    <div id=\"u1-toc\" class=\"section\">\n      <div class=\"sec-head\"><div class=\"sec-icon\">📐</div><div class=\"sec-title\">Branches of Theory of Computation</div><span class=\"badge b-cyan\">Unit 1</span></div>\n      <div class=\"tw\"><table>\n        <thead><tr><th>Branch</th><th>Studies</th><th>Tools</th></tr></thead>\n        <tbody>\n          <tr><td><strong>Automata Theory</strong></td><td>Modeling machines; which languages can be recognized</td><td>DFA, NFA, PDA, TM</td></tr>\n          <tr><td><strong>Computability</strong></td><td>What can be computed at all?</td><td>Recursive functions, Turing Machines</td></tr>\n          <tr><td><strong>Complexity Theory</strong></td><td>How efficiently can a problem be solved?</td><td>Time/space classes, P vs NP</td></tr>\n        </tbody>\n      </table></div>\n      <div class=\"card\"><div class=\"ctitle\">🏗️ Chomsky Hierarchy</div>\n        <div class=\"cb\">Type 3 — Regular Grammars         → Finite Automata (FA)\nType 2 — Context-Free Grammars    → Pushdown Automata (PDA)\nType 1 — Context-Sensitive        → Linear Bounded Automata (LBA)\nType 0 — Unrestricted (RE)        → Turing Machine (TM)\n\nFA ⊂ PDA ⊂ LBA ⊂ TM  (strictly nested, each more powerful)</div>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"alert info\"><div class=\"ai\">ℹ️</div><div><strong>Undecidable Problems:</strong> Halting Problem, Post Correspondence Problem, Hilbert's 10th (integer solutions to Diophantine equations).</div></div>\n    </div>\n\n    <!-- U1 STRINGS -->\n    <div id=\"u1-strings\" class=\"section\">\n      <div class=\"sec-head\"><div class=\"sec-icon\">🔤</div><div class=\"sec-title\">Alphabets, Strings &amp; Special Sets</div><span class=\"badge b-cyan\">Unit 1</span></div>\n      <div class=\"def cy\"><div class=\"def-lbl\">Alphabet (Σ)</div>A <strong>finite, non-empty</strong> set of symbols. e.g., Σ = {0,1} or Σ = {a,b,…,z}.</div>\n      <div class=\"def\"><div class=\"def-lbl\">String</div>A <strong>finite</strong> sequence of symbols from Σ. The <em>empty string</em> ε has length 0.</div>\n      <div class=\"g2 mt8\">\n        <div class=\"card\"><div class=\"ctitle\">📏 String Operations</div>\n          <div class=\"tw\"><table>\n            <thead><tr><th>Operation</th><th>Example</th></tr></thead>\n            <tbody>\n              <tr><td><strong>Length |w|</strong></td><td>|aab| = 3, |ε| = 0</td></tr>\n              <tr><td><strong>Concatenation</strong></td><td>ab · cd = abcd; w · ε = w</td></tr>\n              <tr><td><strong>Exponentiation wⁿ</strong></td><td>ab² = abab, w⁰ = ε</td></tr>\n              <tr><td><strong>Reversal wᴿ</strong></td><td>(abc)ᴿ = cba</td></tr>\n              <tr><td><strong>Σᵏ</strong></td><td>All strings of length exactly k; |Σᵏ| = |Σ|ᵏ</td></tr>\n            </tbody>\n          </table></div>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"card\"><div class=\"ctitle\">♾️ Σ* and Σ⁺</div>\n          <div class=\"def am\"><div class=\"def-lbl\">Kleene Closure Σ*</div>Σ* = Σ⁰ ∪ Σ¹ ∪ Σ² ∪ … = ALL strings (including ε)<br>|Σ*| = ∞ always</div>\n          <div class=\"def gr\" style=\"margin-top:8px\"><div class=\"def-lbl\">Positive Closure Σ⁺</div>Σ⁺ = Σ* − {ε} = all non-empty strings<br>Σ⁺ = Σ¹ ∪ Σ² ∪ …</div>\n          <p class=\"mt8\" style=\"font-size:13px\"><code>|Σᵏ| = |Σ|ᵏ</code> &nbsp;|&nbsp; Powerset |2ˢ| = 2^|ˢ|</p>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"alert warn\"><div class=\"ai\">⚠️</div><div><strong>Traps:</strong> Σ⁰ = {ε} (NOT ∅). Also, ∅* = {ε} — Kleene star of empty language is {ε}, not ∅.</div></div>\n    </div>\n\n    <!-- U1 LANGS -->\n    <div id=\"u1-langs\" class=\"section\">\n      <div class=\"sec-head\"><div class=\"sec-icon\">🌐</div><div class=\"sec-title\">Languages &amp; Operations</div><span class=\"badge b-cyan\">Unit 1</span></div>\n      <div class=\"def cy\"><div class=\"def-lbl\">Formal Language</div>Any subset L ⊆ Σ*. Can be finite or infinite. A \"problem\" = deciding membership w ∈ L.</div>\n      <div class=\"tw mt8\"><table>\n        <thead><tr><th>Operation</th><th>Definition</th></tr></thead>\n        <tbody>\n          <tr><td><strong>Union</strong></td><td>L₁ ∪ L₂ = {x | x ∈ L₁ OR x ∈ L₂}</td></tr>\n          <tr><td><strong>Intersection</strong></td><td>L₁ ∩ L₂ = {x | x ∈ L₁ AND x ∈ L₂}</td></tr>\n          <tr><td><strong>Complement</strong></td><td>L̄ = Σ* − L</td></tr>\n          <tr><td><strong>Concatenation</strong></td><td>L₁·L₂ = {xy | x ∈ L₁, y ∈ L₂}</td></tr>\n          <tr><td><strong>Kleene Star L*</strong></td><td>L⁰ ∪ L¹ ∪ L² ∪ … (zero or more concatenations)</td></tr>\n          <tr><td><strong>Reverse Lᴿ</strong></td><td>{wᴿ | w ∈ L}</td></tr>\n        </tbody>\n      </table></div>\n    </div>\n\n    <!-- U1 MATH -->\n    <div id=\"u1-math\" class=\"section\">\n      <div class=\"sec-head\"><div class=\"sec-icon\">📏</div><div class=\"sec-title\">Mathematical Prerequisites</div><span class=\"badge b-cyan\">Unit 1</span></div>\n      <div class=\"g2\">\n        <div class=\"card\"><div class=\"ctitle\">🔢 Set Theory</div>\n          <ul><li>Powerset 2ˢ: all subsets of S; |2ˢ| = 2^|S|</li><li>Relations on A (|A|=n): 2^(n²) possible</li><li>Complement: Ā = U − A (relative to universal set U)</li></ul>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"card\"><div class=\"ctitle\">🔗 Relations &amp; Functions</div>\n          <ul><li>Binary relation R ⊆ A × B</li><li>Inverse: R⁻¹ = {(b,a) | (a,b) ∈ R}</li><li>Composition: S∘R = {(a,c) | ∃b: (a,b)∈R, (b,c)∈S}</li><li>Function: each input has exactly one output</li></ul>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"card mt8\"><div class=\"ctitle\">📊 Proof Techniques</div>\n        <div class=\"g2\">\n          <div><strong>Mathematical Induction:</strong><br>1. Base case: prove P(n₀)<br>2. Inductive step: P(k) → P(k+1)</div>\n          <div><strong>Other Methods:</strong><br>• Proof by Contradiction<br>• Contrapositive (¬Q → ¬P)<br>• Counter-example (to disprove)</div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n\n    <hr class=\"sep\">\n\n    <!-- U2 DFA -->\n    <div id=\"u2-dfa\" class=\"section\">\n      <div class=\"sec-head\"><div class=\"sec-icon\">🤖</div><div class=\"sec-title\">Deterministic Finite Automata (DFA)</div><span class=\"badge b-ind\">Unit 2</span></div>\n      <div class=\"def\"><div class=\"def-lbl\">Formal Definition — DFA (5-tuple)</div>\n        M = (Q, Σ, δ, q₀, F) where:<br>\n        <strong>Q</strong> — finite set of states &nbsp;|&nbsp; <strong>Σ</strong> — finite input alphabet<br>\n        <strong>δ : Q × Σ → Q</strong> — total transition function (exactly one next state)<br>\n        <strong>q₀ ∈ Q</strong> — start state &nbsp;|&nbsp; <strong>F ⊆ Q</strong> — set of accepting states\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"def am mt8\"><div class=\"def-lbl\">Extended Transition δ̂</div>\n        δ̂(q, ε) = q &nbsp;&nbsp; δ̂(q, wa) = δ(δ̂(q, w), a)<br>\n        <strong>L(M)</strong> = {w ∈ Σ* | δ̂(q₀, w) ∈ F}\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"g2 mt8\">\n        <div class=\"card\"><div class=\"ctitle\">Even # of 0s over {0,1}</div>\n          <div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>State</th><th>0</th><th>1</th><th>Accept?</th></tr></thead>\n          <tbody><tr><td><span class=\"strt\">→ q₀</span></td><td>q₁</td><td>q₀</td><td class=\"acc\">✓</td></tr><tr><td>q₁</td><td>q₀</td><td>q₁</td><td></td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n          <p style=\"font-size:12.5px;color:var(--text3)\">q₀=even 0s (accept), q₁=odd 0s</p>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"card\"><div class=\"ctitle\">Strings containing \"aa\" over {a,b}</div>\n          <div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>State</th><th>a</th><th>b</th><th>Accept?</th></tr></thead>\n          <tbody><tr><td><span class=\"strt\">→ q₀</span></td><td>q₁</td><td>q₀</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>q₁</td><td>q₂</td><td>q₀</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>q₂</td><td>q₂</td><td>q₂</td><td class=\"acc\">✓</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n          <p style=\"font-size:12.5px;color:var(--text3)\">q₂ = absorbing accept state</p>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"alert tip\"><div class=\"ai\">💡</div><div>DFA has <strong>exactly one</strong> transition per state per symbol. No ambiguity. Every DFA is also an NFA (but not vice versa until conversion).</div></div>\n    </div>\n\n    <!-- U2 NFA -->\n    <div id=\"u2-nfa\" class=\"section\">\n      <div class=\"sec-head\"><div class=\"sec-icon\">🔀</div><div class=\"sec-title\">NFA &amp; ε-NFA</div><span class=\"badge b-ind\">Unit 2</span></div>\n      <div class=\"def\"><div class=\"def-lbl\">NFA — Key Differences</div>\n        δ : Q × Σ → <strong>2^Q</strong> (returns a SET of states, possibly ∅)<br>\n        Accept if <strong>at least one</strong> computation path reaches a final state.\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"tw mt8\"><table>\n        <thead><tr><th>Feature</th><th>DFA</th><th>NFA</th></tr></thead>\n        <tbody>\n          <tr><td>Transitions per symbol</td><td>Exactly 1</td><td>0, 1, or many</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>δ return type</td><td>Q</td><td>2^Q</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>ε-moves</td><td>❌</td><td>✅ (in ε-NFA)</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Computational power</td><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"acc\">Equal! Both = Regular Languages</td></tr>\n        </tbody>\n      </table></div>\n      <div class=\"def cy mt8\"><div class=\"def-lbl\">ε-closure</div>\n        ε-closure(q) = {q} ∪ all states reachable from q via ε-transitions only.<br>\n        ε-closure({S}) = ⋃{ε-closure(q) | q ∈ S}\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"card mt8\"><div class=\"ctitle\">NFA Example: 3rd symbol from right = 'a'</div>\n        <div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>State</th><th>a</th><th>b</th><th>Accept?</th></tr></thead>\n        <tbody>\n          <tr><td><span class=\"strt\">→ q₀</span></td><td>{q₀,q₁}</td><td>{q₀}</td><td></td></tr>\n          <tr><td>q₁</td><td>{q₂}</td><td>{q₂}</td><td></td></tr>\n          <tr><td>q₂</td><td>{q₃}</td><td>{q₃}</td><td></td></tr>\n          <tr><td>q₃</td><td>∅</td><td>∅</td><td class=\"acc\">✓</td></tr>\n        </tbody></table></div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n\n    <!-- U2 CONVERT -->\n    <div id=\"u2-convert\" class=\"section\">\n      <div class=\"sec-head\"><div class=\"sec-icon\">🔄</div><div class=\"sec-title\">NFA → DFA (Subset Construction)</div><span class=\"badge b-ind\">Unit 2</span></div>\n      <div class=\"def\"><div class=\"def-lbl\">Algorithm</div>\n        Given NFA M=(Q,Σ,δ,q₀,F), build DFA N=(Q',Σ,δ',q₀',F'):<br>\n        • <strong>q₀'</strong> = ε-closure({q₀}) &nbsp;|&nbsp; <strong>F'</strong> = all DFA states S where S∩F ≠ ∅<br>\n        • <strong>δ'(S,a)</strong> = ε-closure(⋃{δ(q,a) | q ∈ S})\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"card mt8\"><div class=\"ctitle\">Step-by-Step</div>\n        <ol><li>Start state = ε-closure({q₀})</li><li>For each unprocessed DFA state S and each input a: compute δ'(S,a)</li><li>∅ → dead/trap state (self-loops, non-accepting)</li><li>Any DFA state containing NFA accept state → DFA accept state</li><li>Repeat until all states processed</li></ol>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"alert warn\"><div class=\"ai\">⚠️</div><div>Worst case: n NFA states → 2ⁿ DFA states. In practice, usually far fewer reachable states. Only compute <em>reachable</em> states.</div></div>\n      <div class=\"card mt8\"><div class=\"ctitle\">📊 PYP Q5b — ε-NFA → DFA Result</div>\n        <div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>DFA</th><th>NFA States</th><th>0</th><th>1</th><th>Accept?</th></tr></thead>\n        <tbody>\n          <tr><td><span class=\"strt\">A</span></td><td>{q₀,q₁,q₂}</td><td>B</td><td>C</td><td></td></tr>\n          <tr><td>B</td><td>{q₁,q₂,q₃}</td><td>D</td><td>C</td><td></td></tr>\n          <tr><td>C</td><td>{q₁,q₂,q₄}</td><td>B</td><td>E</td><td></td></tr>\n          <tr><td>D</td><td>{q₁,q₂,q₃,q₅,q₆,q₇}</td><td>D</td><td>F</td><td class=\"acc\">✓</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>E</td><td>{q₁,q₂,q₄,q₅,q₆,q₇}</td><td>G</td><td>E</td><td class=\"acc\">✓</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>F</td><td>{q₁,q₂,q₄,q₆,q₇}</td><td>G</td><td>E</td><td class=\"acc\">✓</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>G</td><td>{q₁,q₂,q₃,q₆,q₇}</td><td>D</td><td>F</td><td class=\"acc\">✓</td></tr>\n        </tbody></table></div>\n        <p class=\"mt8\" style=\"font-size:12.5px;color:var(--text3)\">Language: (0+1)*(00+11)(0+1)* — strings containing \"00\" or \"11\"</p>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n\n    <!-- U2 MINIMIZATION -->\n    <div id=\"u2-min\" class=\"section\">\n      <div class=\"sec-head\"><div class=\"sec-icon\">📦</div><div class=\"sec-title\">DFA Minimization (Mark Algorithm)</div><span class=\"badge b-ind\">Unit 2</span></div>\n      <div class=\"def\"><div class=\"def-lbl\">Distinguishable Pairs</div>\n        p ≠ q (distinguishable) if ∃w: exactly one of δ̂(p,w), δ̂(q,w) ∈ F<br>\n        p ≡ q (indistinguishable) if ∀w: δ̂(p,w) ∈ F ↔ δ̂(q,w) ∈ F\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"card mt8\"><div class=\"ctitle\">Mark Procedure (Table-Filling)</div>\n        <ol>\n          <li><strong>Remove inaccessible states</strong> (unreachable from q₀)</li>\n          <li><strong>Base:</strong> Mark (p,q) if one ∈ F and other ∉ F</li>\n          <li><strong>Iterate:</strong> For each unmarked pair (p,q) and each a ∈ Σ:<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;If (δ(p,a), δ(q,a)) is marked → mark (p,q)</li>\n          <li>Repeat step 3 to fixed point</li>\n          <li><strong>Merge</strong> all unmarked (indistinguishable) pairs → equivalence classes</li>\n        </ol>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"card mt8\"><div class=\"ctitle\">📊 PYP Q5a — Minimization Worked Example</div>\n        <div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>State</th><th>0</th><th>1</th><th>Accept?</th></tr></thead>\n        <tbody>\n          <tr><td><span class=\"strt\">→ A</span></td><td>B</td><td>D</td><td></td></tr>\n          <tr><td>B</td><td>B</td><td>C</td><td></td></tr>\n          <tr><td>C</td><td>E</td><td>F</td><td></td></tr>\n          <tr><td>D</td><td>E</td><td>F</td><td></td></tr>\n          <tr><td>E</td><td>E</td><td>F</td><td class=\"acc\">✓</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>F</td><td>F</td><td>F</td><td class=\"acc\">✓</td></tr>\n        </tbody></table></div>\n        <div class=\"def gr mt8\"><div class=\"def-lbl\">Result: 3 Equivalence Classes</div>\n          <strong>C ≡ D</strong> (identical transitions: 0→E, 1→F)<br>\n          <strong>E ≡ F</strong> (both accept, all transitions stay in {E,F})<br>\n          <strong>A ≡ B</strong> (since C≡D: A:1→D≡B:1→C, and A:0→B≡B:0→B)\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"tw mt8\"><table><thead><tr><th>Min. State</th><th>0</th><th>1</th><th>Accept?</th></tr></thead>\n        <tbody>\n          <tr><td><span class=\"strt\">→ P={A,B}</span></td><td>P</td><td>Q</td><td></td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Q={C,D}</td><td>R</td><td>R</td><td></td></tr>\n          <tr><td>R={E,F}</td><td>R</td><td>R</td><td class=\"acc\">✓</td></tr>\n        </tbody></table></div>\n        <p class=\"mt8 tg\" style=\"font-size:13px\">✅ 6 states → 3 states minimized</p>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n\n    <!-- U2 MEALY -->\n    <div id=\"u2-mealy\" class=\"section\">\n      <div class=\"sec-head\"><div class=\"sec-icon\">⚙️</div><div class=\"sec-title\">Moore &amp; Mealy Machines</div><span class=\"badge b-ind\">Unit 2</span></div>\n      <div class=\"tw\"><table>\n        <thead><tr><th>Feature</th><th>Moore Machine</th><th>Mealy Machine</th></tr></thead>\n        <tbody>\n          <tr><td><strong>Output depends on</strong></td><td>State only</td><td>State + Input symbol</td></tr>\n          <tr><td><strong>Output function λ</strong></td><td>λ : Q → Δ</td><td>λ : Q × Σ → Δ</td></tr>\n          <tr><td><strong>When output produced</strong></td><td>On entering a state</td><td>On each transition (arc)</td></tr>\n          <tr><td><strong>Output length</strong></td><td>|input| + 1</td><td>|input|</td></tr>\n          <tr><td><strong>Diagram notation</strong></td><td>Node label: state/output</td><td>Arc label: input/output</td></tr>\n        </tbody>\n      </table></div>\n      <div class=\"g2 mt8\">\n        <div class=\"card\"><div class=\"ctitle\">Mealy → Moore Conversion</div>\n          <ol>\n            <li>Find <strong>incoming output</strong> for each state</li>\n            <li>State with multiple different incoming outputs → <strong>split</strong> into q_z1, q_z2, …</li>\n            <li>Each split state gets output = the arriving output symbol</li>\n            <li>Redirect transitions to appropriate split state</li>\n          </ol>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"card\"><div class=\"ctitle\">Moore → Mealy Conversion</div>\n          <ol>\n            <li>For each arc p →(a)→ q:</li>\n            <li>Mealy output on arc = Moore output of <strong>destination</strong> q: λ(q)</li>\n            <li>Remove state-based output labels</li>\n            <li>Same number of states, outputs move from states → arcs</li>\n          </ol>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"card mt8\"><div class=\"ctitle\">PYP Q6b — Mealy → Moore (State Splitting)</div>\n        <p style=\"font-size:13px;margin-bottom:8px\">Mealy: q₀:0/z₁→q₂, 1/z₁→q₃ | q₂:0/z₁→q₃, 1/z₁→q₂ | q₃:0/z₂→q₃, 1/z₁→q₂</p>\n        <p style=\"font-size:13px;color:var(--amber)\">q₃ receives z₁ (from q₀, q₂) AND z₂ (from q₃ self-loop) → <strong>split q₃ into q₃ᴬ(z₁) and q₃ᴮ(z₂)</strong></p>\n        <div class=\"tw mt8\"><table><thead><tr><th>Moore State</th><th>Output</th><th>On 0</th><th>On 1</th></tr></thead>\n        <tbody>\n          <tr><td><span class=\"strt\">→ q₀</span></td><td>z₁</td><td>q₂</td><td>q₃ᴬ</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>q₂</td><td>z₁</td><td>q₃ᴬ</td><td>q₂</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>q₃ᴬ</td><td>z₁</td><td>q₃ᴮ</td><td>q₂</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>q₃ᴮ</td><td>z₂</td><td>q₃ᴮ</td><td>q₂</td></tr>\n        </tbody></table></div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n\n    <!-- U2 CLOSURE -->\n    <div id=\"u2-closure\" class=\"section\">\n      <div class=\"sec-head\"><div class=\"sec-icon\">🔒</div><div class=\"sec-title\">Closure Properties of Regular Languages</div><span class=\"badge b-ind\">Unit 2</span></div>\n      <div class=\"tw\"><table>\n        <thead><tr><th>Operation</th><th>Regular Closed?</th><th>Proof Method</th></tr></thead>\n        <tbody>\n          <tr><td>Union</td><td class=\"acc\">✓ YES</td><td>RE: R₁+R₂ or NFA construction</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Concatenation</td><td class=\"acc\">✓ YES</td><td>RE: R₁R₂</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Kleene Star</td><td class=\"acc\">✓ YES</td><td>RE: R*</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Complement</td><td class=\"acc\">✓ YES</td><td>DFA: swap F ↔ Q−F</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Intersection</td><td class=\"acc\">✓ YES</td><td>Cross-product DFA, or De Morgan's</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Difference L₁−L₂</td><td class=\"acc\">✓ YES</td><td>L₁ ∩ L̄₂</td></tr>\n          <tr><td>Reverse</td><td class=\"acc\">✓ YES</td><td>Reverse DFA transitions</td></tr>\n        </tbody>\n      </table></div>\n      <div class=\"card mt8\"><div class=\"ctitle\">Cross-Product DFA (Intersection)</div>\n        <p>Given DFA M₁, M₂ → Build M with Q = Q₁×Q₂:</p>\n        <ul class=\"mt8\"><li>Start: (q₁₀, q₂₀)</li><li>δ((p₁,p₂),a) = (δ₁(p₁,a), δ₂(p₂,a))</li><li>Intersection: F = F₁×F₂</li><li>Union: F = (F₁×Q₂) ∪ (Q₁×F₂)</li></ul>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n\n    <hr class=\"sep\">\n\n    <!-- U3 DEF -->\n    <div id=\"u3-def\" class=\"section\">\n      <div class=\"sec-head\"><div class=\"sec-icon\">✨</div><div class=\"sec-title\">Regular Expressions — Definition</div><span class=\"badge b-pur\">Unit 3</span></div>\n      <div class=\"g2\">\n        <div>\n          <div class=\"def\"><div class=\"def-lbl\">Base Cases</div>\n            <strong>∅</strong> — empty language {}<br>\n            <strong>ε</strong> — language {ε}<br>\n            <strong>a</strong> (∀a∈Σ) — language {a}\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"def am mt8\"><div class=\"def-lbl\">Inductive Cases</div>\n            If E, F are REs:<br>\n            <strong>E + F</strong> → L(E) ∪ L(F) (union)<br>\n            <strong>EF</strong> → L(E)·L(F) (concatenation)<br>\n            <strong>E*</strong> → (L(E))* (Kleene star)\n          </div>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"card\">\n          <div class=\"ctitle\">Operator Precedence</div>\n          <div class=\"fm\">* (star) &gt; concatenation &gt; + (union)</div>\n          <p style=\"font-size:13px\"><code>ab+c</code> means <code>(ab)+c</code>, not <code>a(b+c)</code></p>\n          <div class=\"def gr mt8\"><div class=\"def-lbl\">Shorthand</div>\n            <strong>R⁺</strong> = RR* (one or more)<br>\n            <strong>R?</strong> = ε+R (zero or one)<br>\n            <strong>Rⁿ</strong> = R·R·…·R (n times)\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n\n    <!-- U3 EXAMPLES -->\n    <div id=\"u3-examples\" class=\"section\">\n      <div class=\"sec-head\"><div class=\"sec-icon\">📋</div><div class=\"sec-title\">Regular Expression Examples</div><span class=\"badge b-pur\">Unit 3</span></div>\n      <div class=\"tw\"><table>\n        <thead><tr><th>Regular Expression</th><th>Language Described</th></tr></thead>\n        <tbody>\n          <tr><td><code>01*</code></td><td>Strings: 0, 01, 011, 0111, …</td></tr>\n          <tr><td><code>(0+1)*</code></td><td>All binary strings including ε</td></tr>\n          <tr><td><code>(0+1)*00(0+1)*</code></td><td>All strings containing \"00\"</td></tr>\n          <tr><td><code>(0+1)*011</code></td><td>Strings ending with \"011\"</td></tr>\n          <tr><td><code>0*1*</code></td><td>All 0s before all 1s (including ε, 0*, 1*)</td></tr>\n          <tr><td><code>1(0+1)*0</code></td><td>Starts with 1, ends with 0</td></tr>\n          <tr><td><code>(0+1)*1(0+1)(0+1)</code></td><td>3rd symbol from right is 1</td></tr>\n          <tr><td><code>a(aa)*</code></td><td>Odd number of a's</td></tr>\n          <tr><td><code>(aa)*</code></td><td>Even number of a's (including 0)</td></tr>\n          <tr><td><code>(a+ba)*(ε+b)</code></td><td>Strings over {a,b} NOT containing \"bb\"</td></tr>\n          <tr><td><code>(0+1)*010(0+1)*</code></td><td>Contains \"010\" as substring</td></tr>\n          <tr><td><code>a+b+c+</code></td><td>At least one a, then b's, then c's (non-empty each)</td></tr>\n          <tr><td><code>(0+1)*(00+11)(0+1)*</code></td><td>Contains \"00\" or \"11\"</td></tr>\n          <tr><td><code>(1*01*01*01*)*</code></td><td>Number of 0s is multiple of 3</td></tr>\n          <tr><td><code>ε + (0+1)(0+1)*</code></td><td>All binary strings (= (0+1)*)</td></tr>\n        </tbody>\n      </table></div>\n    </div>\n\n    <!-- U3 EQUIV -->\n    <div id=\"u3-equiv\" class=\"section\">\n      <div class=\"sec-head\"><div class=\"sec-icon\">⚖️</div><div class=\"sec-title\">Equivalence of Regular Expressions</div><span class=\"badge b-pur\">Unit 3</span></div>\n      <div class=\"def\"><div class=\"def-lbl\">Definition</div>R₁ ≡ R₂ iff L(R₁) = L(R₂)</div>\n      <div class=\"tw mt8\"><table>\n        <thead><tr><th>Identity</th><th>Explanation</th></tr></thead>\n        <tbody>\n          <tr><td><code>R + ∅ = R</code></td><td>∅ is the additive identity</td></tr>\n          <tr><td><code>Rε = εR = R</code></td><td>ε is the multiplicative identity</td></tr>\n          <tr><td><code>R∅ = ∅R = ∅</code></td><td>∅ annihilates concatenation</td></tr>\n          <tr><td><code>R** = R*</code></td><td>Star is idempotent</td></tr>\n          <tr><td><code>ε + RR* = R*</code></td><td>R* = ε + R⁺</td></tr>\n          <tr><td><code>(R+S)* = (R*S*)*</code></td><td>Star distributes over union</td></tr>\n          <tr><td><code>R + R = R</code></td><td>Union is idempotent</td></tr>\n          <tr><td><code>(ε+R)* = R*</code></td><td>Adding ε under star changes nothing</td></tr>\n        </tbody>\n      </table></div>\n    </div>\n\n    <!-- U3 FA -->\n    <div id=\"u3-fa\" class=\"section\">\n      <div class=\"sec-head\"><div class=\"sec-icon\">↔️</div><div class=\"sec-title\">RE ↔ Automata Equivalence</div><span class=\"badge b-pur\">Unit 3</span></div>\n      <div class=\"def gr\"><div class=\"def-lbl\">Main Theorem</div>\n        <strong>DFA = NFA = ε-NFA = Regular Expression</strong><br>\n        All describe exactly the class of <em>Regular Languages</em>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"card mt8\"><div class=\"ctitle\">Thompson's Construction: RE → ε-NFA</div>\n        <div class=\"cb\">Base:   ∅ → [s]      ε → [s] →ε→ [f]      a → [s] →a→ [f]\n\nUnion (R+S):\n         ε→[Mᴿ]→ε\n[new_s]→             →[new_f]\n         ε→[Mₛ]→ε\n\nConcatenation (RS):\n[Mᴿ] →ε→ [Mₛ]   (connect accept of R to start of S)\n\nStar (R*):\n         ε (bypass)\n[ns]→ε→[Mᴿ]→ε→[nf]\n         ↑──ε──┘ (loop back)</div>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"def cy mt8\"><div class=\"def-lbl\">FA → RE (State Elimination)</div>\n        1. Add new global start and accept states with ε-transitions<br>\n        2. Eliminate intermediate states: replace with equivalent RE on remaining arcs<br>\n        3. Final RE = label on arc from global-start to global-accept\n      </div>\n    </div>\n\n    <hr class=\"sep\">\n\n    <!-- PYP -->\n    <div id=\"pyp\" class=\"section\">\n      <div class=\"sec-head\"><div class=\"sec-icon\">📄</div><div class=\"sec-title\">Previous Year Paper T1 — Full Solutions</div><span class=\"badge b-amb\">16 Marks</span></div>\n\n      <div class=\"pyq\"><div class=\"pyqh\"><span class=\"pyqn\">Q1a · 1M</span><div class=\"pyqt\">Given Σ={x,y,z}. How many different strings of length up to 2 can be formed including ε?</div></div>\n        <div class=\"pya\"><div class=\"pyal\">✅ Solution</div>\n          <div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Length</th><th>Count</th></tr></thead>\n          <tbody><tr><td>0 (ε)</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>|Σ|¹ = 3</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>|Σ|² = 9</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n          <div class=\"fm\">Total = 1 + 3 + 9 = 13 strings</div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n\n      <div class=\"pyq\"><div class=\"pyqh\"><span class=\"pyqn\">Q1b · 1M</span><div class=\"pyqt\">Find prefix and suffix of length up to 3 for the string \"abaabbab\".</div></div>\n        <div class=\"pya\"><div class=\"pyal\">✅ Solution</div>\n          <strong>Prefixes:</strong> ε, a, ab, aba &nbsp;|&nbsp; <strong>Suffixes:</strong> ε, b, ab, bab\n        </div>\n      </div>\n\n      <div class=\"pyq\"><div class=\"pyqh\"><span class=\"pyqn\">Q2 · 2M</span><div class=\"pyqt\">L1={ε}, L2={a}, L3={∅}. Compute L1·L2* ∪ L3*.</div></div>\n        <div class=\"pya\"><div class=\"pyal\">✅ Solution</div>\n          L2* = a* &nbsp;→&nbsp; L1·L2* = {ε}·a* = a*<br>\n          L3* = ∅* = {ε} &nbsp;(Kleene star of empty language)<br>\n          a* ∪ {ε} = <strong>a*</strong> (ε ∈ a* already)\n        </div>\n      </div>\n\n      <div class=\"pyq\"><div class=\"pyqh\"><span class=\"pyqn\">Q3 · 2M</span><div class=\"pyqt\">DFA over {a,b}: at least one 'a' AND exactly two 'b's.</div></div>\n        <div class=\"pya\"><div class=\"pyal\">✅ Solution — 7 States (track b-count × has-a)</div>\n          <div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>State</th><th>b-count</th><th>a seen?</th><th>a</th><th>b</th><th>Accept?</th></tr></thead>\n          <tbody>\n            <tr><td><span class=\"strt\">→ q₀₀</span></td><td>0</td><td>No</td><td>q₀₁</td><td>q₁₀</td><td></td></tr>\n            <tr><td>q₀₁</td><td>0</td><td>Yes</td><td>q₀₁</td><td>q₁₁</td><td></td></tr>\n            <tr><td>q₁₀</td><td>1</td><td>No</td><td>q₁₁</td><td>q₂₀</td><td></td></tr>\n            <tr><td>q₁₁</td><td>1</td><td>Yes</td><td>q₁₁</td><td>q₂₁</td><td></td></tr>\n            <tr><td>q₂₀</td><td>2</td><td>No</td><td>q₂₁</td><td>qd</td><td></td></tr>\n            <tr><td><strong>q₂₁</strong></td><td>2</td><td>Yes</td><td>q₂₁</td><td>qd</td><td class=\"acc\">✓</td></tr>\n            <tr><td>qd</td><td>3+</td><td>—</td><td>qd</td><td>qd</td><td></td></tr>\n          </tbody></table></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n\n      <div class=\"pyq\"><div class=\"pyqh\"><span class=\"pyqn\">Q4 · 2M</span><div class=\"pyqt\">NFA over {a,b}: third symbol from right is 'a'. RE: (a+b)*a(a+b)(a+b)</div></div>\n        <div class=\"pya\"><div class=\"pyal\">✅ Solution — 4 States</div>\n          <div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>State</th><th>a</th><th>b</th><th>Accept?</th></tr></thead>\n          <tbody>\n            <tr><td><span class=\"strt\">→ q₀</span></td><td>{q₀,q₁}</td><td>{q₀}</td><td></td></tr>\n            <tr><td>q₁</td><td>{q₂}</td><td>{q₂}</td><td></td></tr>\n            <tr><td>q₂</td><td>{q₃}</td><td>{q₃}</td><td></td></tr>\n            <tr><td>q₃</td><td>∅</td><td>∅</td><td class=\"acc\">✓</td></tr>\n          </tbody></table></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n\n      <div class=\"pyq\"><div class=\"pyqh\"><span class=\"pyqn\">Q5a · 4M</span><div class=\"pyqt\">Construct Minimized DFA from given DFA (A=start, E/F=accept).</div></div>\n        <div class=\"pya\"><div class=\"pyal\">✅ Mark Algorithm → 3 States</div>\n          <strong>C≡D</strong> (both: 0→E, 1→F) &nbsp;|&nbsp; <strong>E≡F</strong> (both accept, all→{E,F}) &nbsp;|&nbsp; <strong>A≡B</strong> (since C≡D)\n          <div class=\"tw mt8\"><table><thead><tr><th>Min. State</th><th>0</th><th>1</th><th>Accept?</th></tr></thead>\n          <tbody>\n            <tr><td><span class=\"strt\">→ P={A,B}</span></td><td>P</td><td>Q</td><td></td></tr>\n            <tr><td>Q={C,D}</td><td>R</td><td>R</td><td></td></tr>\n            <tr><td>R={E,F}</td><td>R</td><td>R</td><td class=\"acc\">✓</td></tr>\n          </tbody></table></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n\n      <div class=\"pyq\"><div class=\"pyqh\"><span class=\"pyqn\">Q5b · 4M</span><div class=\"pyqt\">Construct DFA from given ε-NFA (q₀→ε→q₁→ε→q₂, q₁ loops, q₂:0→q₃/1→q₄, q₃:0→q₅, q₄:1→q₅, q₅→ε→q₆→ε→q₇, q₆ loops, q₇ accept).</div></div>\n        <div class=\"pya\"><div class=\"pyal\">✅ Subset Construction — 7 DFA States</div>\n          <div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>DFA</th><th>NFA States</th><th>0</th><th>1</th><th>Accept?</th></tr></thead>\n          <tbody>\n            <tr><td><span class=\"strt\">A</span></td><td>{q₀,q₁,q₂}</td><td>B</td><td>C</td><td></td></tr>\n            <tr><td>B</td><td>{q₁,q₂,q₃}</td><td>D</td><td>C</td><td></td></tr>\n            <tr><td>C</td><td>{q₁,q₂,q₄}</td><td>B</td><td>E</td><td></td></tr>\n            <tr><td>D</td><td>{q₁,q₂,q₃,q₅,q₆,q₇}</td><td>D</td><td>F</td><td class=\"acc\">✓</td></tr>\n            <tr><td>E</td><td>{q₁,q₂,q₄,q₅,q₆,q₇}</td><td>G</td><td>E</td><td class=\"acc\">✓</td></tr>\n            <tr><td>F</td><td>{q₁,q₂,q₄,q₆,q₇}</td><td>G</td><td>E</td><td class=\"acc\">✓</td></tr>\n            <tr><td>G</td><td>{q₁,q₂,q₃,q₆,q₇}</td><td>D</td><td>F</td><td class=\"acc\">✓</td></tr>\n          </tbody></table></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n\n      <div class=\"pyq\"><div class=\"pyqh\"><span class=\"pyqn\">Q6a · 2M</span><div class=\"pyqt\">Mealy Machine: output \"A\" if ends with \"10\", \"B\" if ends with \"11\", \"C\" otherwise.</div></div>\n        <div class=\"pya\"><div class=\"pyal\">✅ 2 States</div>\n          <div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>State</th><th>Input</th><th>Output</th><th>Next</th></tr></thead>\n          <tbody>\n            <tr><td><span class=\"strt\">→ q₀</span></td><td>0</td><td>C</td><td>q₀</td></tr>\n            <tr><td><span class=\"strt\">→ q₀</span></td><td>1</td><td>C</td><td>q₁</td></tr>\n            <tr><td>q₁ (last=1)</td><td>0</td><td class=\"ta\">A</td><td>q₀</td></tr>\n            <tr><td>q₁ (last=1)</td><td>1</td><td class=\"tg\">B</td><td>q₁</td></tr>\n          </tbody></table></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n\n      <div class=\"pyq\"><div class=\"pyqh\"><span class=\"pyqn\">Q6b · 2M</span><div class=\"pyqt\">Convert given Mealy Machine (q₀,q₂,q₃; outputs z₁,z₂) to Moore Machine.</div></div>\n        <div class=\"pya\"><div class=\"pyal\">✅ Split q₃ → q₃ᴬ(z₁) and q₃ᴮ(z₂)</div>\n          <div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>Moore State</th><th>λ (Output)</th><th>On 0</th><th>On 1</th></tr></thead>\n          <tbody>\n            <tr><td><span class=\"strt\">→ q₀</span></td><td>z₁</td><td>q₂</td><td>q₃ᴬ</td></tr>\n            <tr><td>q₂</td><td>z₁</td><td>q₃ᴬ</td><td>q₂</td></tr>\n            <tr><td>q₃ᴬ</td><td>z₁</td><td>q₃ᴮ</td><td>q₂</td></tr>\n            <tr><td>q₃ᴮ</td><td>z₂</td><td>q₃ᴮ</td><td>q₂</td></tr>\n          </tbody></table></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n\n    <hr class=\"sep\">\n\n    <!-- SAMPLE PAPERS -->\n    <div id=\"papers\" class=\"section\">\n      <div class=\"sec-head\"><div class=\"sec-icon\">📝</div><div class=\"sec-title\">Sample Question Papers (4 × 6 Questions)</div><span class=\"badge b-grn\">Practice</span></div>\n      <div class=\"ptabs\">\n        <div class=\"ptab at\" onclick=\"showPaper(0)\">📄 Paper 1</div>\n        <div class=\"ptab\" onclick=\"showPaper(1)\">📄 Paper 2</div>\n        <div class=\"ptab\" onclick=\"showPaper(2)\">📄 Paper 3</div>\n        <div class=\"ptab\" onclick=\"showPaper(3)\">📄 Paper 4</div>\n      </div>\n\n      <!-- PAPER 1 -->\n      <div class=\"pc show\" id=\"p0\">\n        <div class=\"alert info\" style=\"margin-bottom:16px\"><div class=\"ai\">📋</div><div><strong>Paper 1 — Theory &amp; Construction Focus</strong> | Pattern: 1+1+2+2+4+4 = 14 Marks</div></div>\n\n        <div class=\"qcard\"><div class=\"qhdr\" onclick=\"toggleQ(this)\"><div class=\"qnum\">1a</div><div class=\"qtxt\">Given Σ={0,1,2}, how many strings of length ≤ 3 can be formed including ε?</div><div class=\"qmeta\"><span class=\"mb2\">1 Mark</span><span class=\"cb2\">CO1</span></div></div>\n          <div class=\"qbody\" style=\"display:none\"><button class=\"tbtn\" onclick=\"toggleAns(this)\">Show Answer</button>\n            <div class=\"qans\" style=\"display:none\"><div class=\"qans-lbl\">Answer</div>\n              |Σ|=3. Total = 3⁰+3¹+3²+3³ = 1+3+9+27 = <strong>40 strings</strong>\n            </div>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <div class=\"qcard\"><div class=\"qhdr\" onclick=\"toggleQ(this)\"><div class=\"qnum\">1b</div><div class=\"qtxt\">List all prefixes and suffixes of length ≤ 2 for string \"abba\".</div><div class=\"qmeta\"><span class=\"mb2\">1 Mark</span><span class=\"cb2\">CO1</span></div></div>\n          <div class=\"qbody\" style=\"display:none\"><button class=\"tbtn\" onclick=\"toggleAns(this)\">Show Answer</button>\n            <div class=\"qans\" style=\"display:none\"><div class=\"qans-lbl\">Answer</div>\n              <strong>Prefixes (len≤2):</strong> ε, a, ab &nbsp;|&nbsp; <strong>Suffixes (len≤2):</strong> ε, a, ba\n            </div>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <div class=\"qcard\"><div class=\"qhdr\" onclick=\"toggleQ(this)\"><div class=\"qnum\">2</div><div class=\"qtxt\">For L1={a}, L2={b}, L3={ε}, compute (L1∪L2)* and L1·L2*. State if results are regular.</div><div class=\"qmeta\"><span class=\"mb2\">2 Marks</span><span class=\"cb2\">CO1</span></div></div>\n          <div class=\"qbody\" style=\"display:none\"><button class=\"tbtn\" onclick=\"toggleAns(this)\">Show Answer</button>\n            <div class=\"qans\" style=\"display:none\"><div class=\"qans-lbl\">Answer</div>\n              <strong>(L1∪L2)*</strong> = {a,b}* = all strings over {a,b} including ε. RE: (a+b)*<br>\n              <strong>L1·L2*</strong> = {a}·{ε,b,bb,…} = {a,ab,abb,abbb,…} = ab*<br>\n              Both are <strong>regular</strong> languages.\n            </div>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <div class=\"qcard\"><div class=\"qhdr\" onclick=\"toggleQ(this)\"><div class=\"qnum\">3</div><div class=\"qtxt\">Construct DFA over Σ={0,1} accepting strings with even number of 0s AND even number of 1s.</div><div class=\"qmeta\"><span class=\"mb2\">2 Marks</span><span class=\"cb2\">CO2</span></div></div>\n          <div class=\"qbody\" style=\"display:none\"><p style=\"font-size:13px\">Hint: 4 states tracking (parity of 0s, parity of 1s)</p><button class=\"tbtn\" onclick=\"toggleAns(this)\">Show Answer</button>\n            <div class=\"qans\" style=\"display:none\"><div class=\"qans-lbl\">Answer — 4 States</div>\n              <div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>State</th><th>#0 even?</th><th>#1 even?</th><th>0</th><th>1</th><th>Accept?</th></tr></thead>\n              <tbody>\n                <tr><td><span class=\"strt\">→ q₀₀</span></td><td>Yes</td><td>Yes</td><td>q₁₀</td><td>q₀₁</td><td class=\"acc\">✓</td></tr>\n                <tr><td>q₀₁</td><td>Yes</td><td>No</td><td>q₁₁</td><td>q₀₀</td><td></td></tr>\n                <tr><td>q₁₀</td><td>No</td><td>Yes</td><td>q₀₀</td><td>q₁₁</td><td></td></tr>\n                <tr><td>q₁₁</td><td>No</td><td>No</td><td>q₀₁</td><td>q₁₀</td><td></td></tr>\n              </tbody></table></div>\n            </div>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <div class=\"qcard\"><div class=\"qhdr\" onclick=\"toggleQ(this)\"><div class=\"qnum\">4</div><div class=\"qtxt\">Construct NFA over Σ={a,b} accepting all strings ending in \"ab\".</div><div class=\"qmeta\"><span class=\"mb2\">2 Marks</span><span class=\"cb2\">CO2</span></div></div>\n          <div class=\"qbody\" style=\"display:none\"><p style=\"font-size:13px\">RE: (a+b)*ab</p><button class=\"tbtn\" onclick=\"toggleAns(this)\">Show Answer</button>\n            <div class=\"qans\" style=\"display:none\"><div class=\"qans-lbl\">Answer — 3 States</div>\n              <div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>State</th><th>a</th><th>b</th><th>Accept?</th></tr></thead>\n              <tbody>\n                <tr><td><span class=\"strt\">→ q₀</span></td><td>{q₀,q₁}</td><td>{q₀}</td><td></td></tr>\n                <tr><td>q₁</td><td>∅</td><td>{q₂}</td><td></td></tr>\n                <tr><td>q₂</td><td>∅</td><td>∅</td><td class=\"acc\">✓</td></tr>\n              </tbody></table></div>\n            </div>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <div class=\"qcard\"><div class=\"qhdr\" onclick=\"toggleQ(this)\"><div class=\"qnum\">5</div><div class=\"qtxt\">Minimize DFA (Σ={0,1}): States {A,B,C,D,E}, Start=A, Accept={D,E}. A:0→B,1→C | B:0→D,1→A | C:0→A,1→D | D:0→D,1→E | E:0→E,1→D.</div><div class=\"qmeta\"><span class=\"mb2\">4 Marks</span><span class=\"cb2\">CO2</span></div></div>\n          <div class=\"qbody\" style=\"display:none\"><button class=\"tbtn\" onclick=\"toggleAns(this)\">Show Answer</button>\n            <div class=\"qans\" style=\"display:none\"><div class=\"qans-lbl\">Answer</div>\n              <strong>Base marking:</strong> (A,D),(A,E),(B,D),(B,E),(C,D),(C,E)<br>\n              <strong>Check (D,E):</strong> D:0→D, E:0→E → (D,E); D:1→E, E:1→D → (E,D)=(D,E) — not newly marked → <strong>D ≡ E</strong><br>\n              <strong>Check (A,B):</strong> A:0→B, B:0→D → (B,D) marked → A ≠ B<br>\n              <strong>Check (A,C):</strong> A:0→B, C:0→A → (B,A)=(A,B) → check: A:0→B(non-acc), B:0→D(acc) → marked → A ≠ C<br>\n              <strong>Check (B,C):</strong> B:0→D, C:0→A → (D,A)=(A,D) marked → B ≠ C<br>\n              Only D≡E. Minimized 4-state DFA:\n              <div class=\"tw mt8\"><table><thead><tr><th>State</th><th>0</th><th>1</th><th>Accept?</th></tr></thead>\n              <tbody>\n                <tr><td><span class=\"strt\">→ A</span></td><td>B</td><td>C</td><td></td></tr>\n                <tr><td>B</td><td>DE</td><td>A</td><td></td></tr>\n                <tr><td>C</td><td>A</td><td>DE</td><td></td></tr>\n                <tr><td>DE</td><td>DE</td><td>DE</td><td class=\"acc\">✓</td></tr>\n              </tbody></table></div>\n            </div>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <div class=\"qcard\"><div class=\"qhdr\" onclick=\"toggleQ(this)\"><div class=\"qnum\">6</div><div class=\"qtxt\">Design Mealy Machine over {0,1}: outputs '1' if count of 1s seen so far is divisible by 3, else outputs '0'. Then convert to Moore Machine.</div><div class=\"qmeta\"><span class=\"mb2\">4 Marks</span><span class=\"cb2\">CO2</span></div></div>\n          <div class=\"qbody\" style=\"display:none\"><button class=\"tbtn\" onclick=\"toggleAns(this)\">Show Answer</button>\n            <div class=\"qans\" style=\"display:none\"><div class=\"qans-lbl\">Answer — Mealy (3 States tracking count mod 3)</div>\n              <div class=\"tw\"><table><thead><tr><th>State</th><th>Input</th><th>Output</th><th>Next</th></tr></thead>\n              <tbody>\n                <tr><td><span class=\"strt\">→ q₀ (0 mod 3)</span></td><td>0</td><td class=\"tg\">1</td><td>q₀</td></tr>\n                <tr><td>q₀</td><td>1</td><td>0</td><td>q₁</td></tr>\n                <tr><td>q₁ (1 mod 3)</td><td>0</td><td>0</td><td>q₁</td></tr>\n                <tr><td>q₁</td><td>1</td><td>0</td><td>q₂</td></tr>\n                <tr><td>q₂ (2 mod 3)</td><td>0</td><td>0</td><td>q₂</td></tr>\n                <tr><td>q₂</td><td>1</td><td class=\"tg\">1</td><td>q₀</td></tr>\n              </tbody></table></div>\n              <p class=\"mt8\"><strong>Moore conversion:</strong> q₀ receives: 1 (from q₂ via '1'), 0 (self on '0'). Split into q₀ᴬ(output=1) and q₀ᴮ(output=0 for start). q₁, q₂ always receive output=0, no split needed.</p>\n            </div>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n\n      <!-- PAPER 2 -->\n      <div class=\"pc\" id=\"p1\">\n        <div class=\"alert info\" style=\"margin-bottom:16px\"><div class=\"ai\">📋</div><div><strong>Paper 2 — NFA, ε-NFA &amp; Language Operations Focus</strong> | 14 Marks</div></div>\n\n        <div class=\"qcard\"><div class=\"qhdr\" onclick=\"toggleQ(this)\"><div class=\"qnum\">1a</div><div class=\"qtxt\">State the formal definition of a DFA. What does L(M) denote?</div><div class=\"qmeta\"><span class=\"mb2\">1 Mark</span><span class=\"cb2\">CO1</span></div></div>\n          <div class=\"qbody\" style=\"